    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33878" root="فسكل" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِسْكِلٌ</span></b>  The <i>last, in coming in, of the horses in a
race;</i> (S, O, K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُسْكُلٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُسْكُولٌ</span></b>  and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَسْكَوْلٌ</span></b> : (K:) also called the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُكَّيْت</span> [q. v.] and
the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَاشُور</span>. (S, O. [In a copy of the S, in art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سكت</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الفِسْكِلُّ</span> is put for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الفِسْكِلُ</span>.]) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And hence,
(S, O,) applied to a man, (assumed tropical:)  <i>Low, base, ignoble,
vile,</i> or <i>mean:</i> (S, O, K:) the vulgar say ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُسْكُلٌ</span></b> .
(S, O.)

